As you almost certainly know, once the Wizard of Yendor dies for the
first time (or once you do the invocation, whichever comes first), he
harasses you for the rest of the game: random curses, reappearances,
summonings of monsters, vague nervousness, that sort of thing.

A few turns after opening the Sanctum, you're guaranteed to get a Wizard
action. However, although this action is often Wizard reappearance
(that's why you're seeing him in the Sanctum so often), it doesn't have
to be; if, say, he'd cursed your items, you might have assumed that was
a monster spell instead (the two look identical), and you may well have
dismissed a feeling of vague nervousness (because, after all, it doesn't
actually do anything). So this game, he must have decided to do
something else instead.

When the Wizard does reappear, his AI is set to prioritise going for the
Amulet, and (being covetous) he can teleport ignoring no-teleport
restrictions. As such, if he happens to reappear in the Sanctum and you
haven't had much chance to disturb the layout yet (because he's
guaranteed to act a few turns after Sanctum opening), he's likely to
teleport into the temple because that's where the Amulet is.

There is, however, no guarantee you'll meet him any more than the two
guaranteed appearances (in his tower when you get the Book, and on
Earth). Incidentally, the appearance on Earth is avoidable, but it
requires paralyzing him on another level then getting to Earth before
the paralysis wears off; this isn't a very common thing for players to
do, so most people don't know it can be done.

